Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 00:28:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] ASoC: AKM AK4961 codec, AK49xx core and msm8996-ak496x
 machine driver (axon7)

From the ZTE 3.18 kernel, ported to the 4.4 ASoC API:
- widget->codec -> snd_soc_dapm_to_codec(), codec->dapm ->
  snd_soc_codec_get_dapm(), codec->mutex -> a driver mutex
- the ASoC codec register cache is gone: ak4961 keeps its own (with the
  re-write after reset that snd_soc_cache_sync did)
- regulator_set_optimum_mode -> regulator_set_load, set_irq_flags ->
  irq_clear_status_flags, no spi_driver suspend/resume
- snd_soc_jack_new -> snd_soc_card_jack_new
- msm_is_in_voice_call() (ZTE) in msm-pcm-routing-v2
The machine driver replaces msm8996.c (the WCD9335 is not fitted).

